From c702d536818c28861d6dee2be8a9ee85b2403c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Iwanicki?= <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:29:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tpmlib: treat an all-ones TPM_ACCESS read as not granted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tis_request_locality() takes a locality as granted when activeLocality
is set in its TPM_ACCESS register. A locality the chipset does not
decode for the host reads as all ones, which sets that bit too, so the
SKL could believe it held a locality it cannot use.

Reserved bit 6 is set in that value, so treat an all-ones read as not
granted.

This is the tis.c part of "amdsl: hold no TPM locality during
DRTM_CMD_LAUNCH", which applies on every launch path, not only the
AMDSL build.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Signed-off-by: Michał Kopeć <michal.kopec@3mdeb.com>
---
 tpmlib/tis.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tpmlib/tis.c b/tpmlib/tis.c
index 4547735..63ca86c 100644
--- a/tpmlib/tis.c
+++ b/tpmlib/tis.c
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ void tis_relinquish_locality(void)
 
 u8 tis_request_locality(u8 l)
 {
+	u8 access;
+
 	if (l > TPM_MAX_LOCALITY)
 		return TPM_NO_LOCALITY;
 
@@ -68,8 +70,12 @@ u8 tis_request_locality(u8 l)
 
 	tpm_write8(ACCESS_REQUEST_USE, ACCESS(l));
 
-	/* wait for locality to be granted */
-	if (tpm_read8(ACCESS(l)) & ACCESS_ACTIVE_LOCALITY)
+	/*
+	 * A locality the chipset does not decode for the host reads as all
+	 * ones, which has the reserved bit 6 set. Treat that as not granted.
+	 */
+	access = tpm_read8(ACCESS(l));
+	if (access != 0xff && (access & ACCESS_ACTIVE_LOCALITY))
 		locality = l;
 
 	return locality;
-- 
